=(_:_:)"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge":{"title":"MXLWedge","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLWedge","abstract":[{"text":"The wedge type represents crescendo and diminuendo wedge symbols. The type attribute is crescendo for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start of a wedge that is closed at the left side, and diminuendo for the start of a wedge that is closed on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the right side. Spread values are measured in tenths; those at the start of a crescendo wedge or end of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"diminuendo wedge are ignored. The niente attribute is yes if a circle appears at the point of the wedge,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicating a crescendo from nothing or diminuendo to nothing. It is no by default, and used only when the type","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is crescendo, or the type is stop for a wedge that began with a diminuendo type. The line-type is solid if not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specified.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLWedge","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLWedge/Kind-swift.enum/!=(_:_:)":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"!="},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlwedge\/kind-swift.enum\/!=(_:_: